## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `qwen3.7-max` / `qwen/qwen3.7-max` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists Qwen3.7 Max as a proprietary Alibaba reasoning model (released May 2026, deprecated in AA view with suggestion to consider Qwen3.8 Max), supporting text input and text output, with 1M-token context window, pricing around $2.50/$7.50 per 1M tokens (cache discount 80%), TTFA ~14.28s and output speed ~157 tok/s in AA snapshots. OpenRouter lists `qwen/qwen3.7-max` with provider routing and parameter support.
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot; no standalone verified benchmark scores (e.g. GPQA, SWE-bench, HLE, MMMU, Terminal-Bench, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.) for this exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

